<!--
  Mareco: every text shown in the app lives here, so it can be translated.

  Rules for translators (also checked by the unit test StringsTest):
   - Keep every placeholder (%s, %1$s, %2$s ...) and the symbols ▶ ■ ● → · … × ±.
   - Placeholders may be moved or re-ordered (use %1$s / %2$s) but never removed.
   - Do not use the straight quote characters ' and " inside a text: use ’ and “ ” (or your language's quotes).
   - \n means a new line. %% means a literal percent sign.
   - Keep short labels short: they have to fit on small buttons.
-->
