    <!-- Use the names Android itself uses in your language for “Installed apps” / “Downloaded apps”. -->
    <string name="setup_steps">1. Tap the button below.\n2. Open “Installed apps” or “Downloaded apps”.\n3. Choose Mareco and switch it on.\n4. Come back here.</string>
    <string name="setup_open_settings">Open Android Settings</string>
    <string name="setup_after">After enabling the permission:</string>
    <string name="setup_why_title">What the permission is for</string>
    <string name="setup_why_a11y">Accessibility service: the only way Android lets an app tap and swipe for you. Mareco uses it to draw the floating controls, to put an invisible layer on screen while you record, and to replay your gestures. It cannot read your screen, your passwords or your messages.</string>
    <string name="setup_why_keys">Button presses: only while recording or running, so Mareco can record Back / Home / Recents and notice the Volume Up + Volume Down emergency stop. Typed text is never stored.</string>
    <string name="setup_why_app">Which app is in front: used only for the optional “Only run while this app is open” safety.</string>
    <string name="setup_no_internet">Mareco has no internet permission at all, so nothing can leave your phone.</string>
    <string name="setup_grey_title">The switch is greyed out?</string>
    <!-- Use the names Android itself uses in your language for “Allow restricted settings”. -->
    <string name="setup_grey_body">Android 13 and newer block sideloaded apps from using accessibility until you allow it:\n1. Tap “Open App info”.\n2. Tap the three dots at the top right.\n3. Choose “Allow restricted settings” and confirm.\n4. Go back and enable the service.</string>
    <string name="setup_open_app_info">Open App info</string>
    <string name="setup_keep_title">Keep it running</string>
    <string name="setup_keep_body">For long sessions set Mareco’s battery usage to “Unrestricted” (App info → Battery) and keep the charger connected. While a macro runs Mareco keeps the screen on.</string>

    <!-- ===== Help screen ===== -->
    <string name="help_title">Help and limitations</string>
    <string name="help_bar_title">The floating bar</string>
    <string name="help_bar_play">Blue ● / ▶ button: starts recording (Record mode) or runs your macro (Start mode). While recording or running it becomes ■: press it to stop. After a recording it asks you to name and save it.</string>
    <string name="help_bar_hold">Hold the blue button: pause or resume (while recording or running), or stop (while paused).</string>
    <string name="help_bar_gear">Gear: choose Record macro or Start macro mode, pick your default macro, change its execution settings and every other setting.</string>
    <string name="help_bar_move">Four arrows: drag the bar anywhere. X: close the bar (open it again from the app). Long-press a button to see its name.</string>
    <string name="help_flow_title">Record, stop, configure, execute</string>
    <string name="help_flow_body">1. In Mareco, press Start Recording. The floating bar appears.\n2. Open your game.\n3. Press the blue ● when you are ready.\n4. Do your actions normally.\n5. Press ■ and give the macro a name.\n6. Gear → Start macro, tune the execution settings and press ▶.\nStop any time with ■, the STOP button in the app, or Volume Up + Volume Down together.</string>
    <string name="help_live_title">Live and Plan recording</string>
    <string name="help_live_body">Live (default): Mareco records your touches and replays each gesture to the app right after you lift your finger, so the game reacts while you record.</string>
    <string name="help_plan_body">Plan: touches are only recorded; the app does not react. Use it if Live causes trouble.</string>
    <string name="help_limits_title">What Android does not allow</string>
    <string name="help_limit_1">• An app cannot watch touches that go to another app. That is why recording uses a transparent layer and replays your gestures. A new touch in the split second while a gesture is being replayed can be missed, so avoid extremely fast repeated taps while recording, or use Plan mode.</string>
    <string name="help_limit_2">• Some screens block automated gestures: password fields, banking apps and apps that block accessibility tools.</string>
    <string name="help_limit_3">• Only Back, Home and Recents can be recorded as button presses. Volume, camera and other keys cannot be replayed.</string>
    <string name="help_limit_4">• Nothing runs while the screen is off or locked. Mareco keeps the screen on during a macro and stops if it turns off.</string>
    <string name="help_limit_5">• Record and replay in the same orientation. If the screen size differs, Mareco scales coordinates and warns you.</string>
    <string name="help_limit_6">• Android may stop apps in the background to save battery. Set Mareco’s battery usage to Unrestricted for long sessions.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_body">Mareco has no internet permission. Macros are .mareco files stored privately on your phone; you choose when to share one.</string>

